        "original_id": "f7863135-0386-5d91-bc67-13207ee27478",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Coll, Loch Breachacha, Scotland\n- Structures: Breachacha Castle, Breacachadh Castle, Dùn Dubh, hillfort, sand dunes\n- Wildlife: corncrakes\n\nFacts:\n- Coll is known for sandy beaches that rise to form large sand dunes.\n- Coll is known for corncrakes.\n- Coll is known for Breacachadh Castle.\n- Breachacha Castle, also spelled Breacachadh, refers to either of two structures on the shore of Loch Breachacha on the Inner Hebridean island of Coll, Scotland.\n- Dùn Dubh is a hillfort on the Inner Hebridean island of Coll.",
